{#- Deterministic (no-LLM) symbol spotlight.

    "Where it is used" reads only what the resolver resolved to this symbol:
    calls, heritage and dispatch, the uses selection ranked it by. Production
    uses are listed and calls from tests are counted,
    since a hub's list is otherwise two dozen test helpers. With nothing
    resolved the section says so in one line: the files importing the defining
    module are on the file page, and listing them here called twenty-five
    importers of ``parser.py`` the users of a constant they never touch.

    The list stops at 25, the same bound ``file_page.j2`` puts on "Used by",
    while the summary line keeps the true total.

    No source copy: an agent reads the body with ``get_symbol`` or from the
    file, and a copy here went stale with every edit to it. No question block
    or footer either: neither said anything this page's identifiers do not.

    The Overview's no-docstring sentence stays even though it reads like a
    placeholder. It is what ``_extract_summary`` reads back as the page
    summary, and it names the symbol, its kind and its file.
-#}
{#- The symbol's own name, not the synthetic dotted path built by joining
    every directory above it. The file it lives in is on the line below, which
    is where a reader looks for it and is the form ``get_symbol`` takes.
-#}
